/-!
# Recovering a finite graded module from its associated sheaf in high degrees

Source: Stacks Project, coherent.tex, Tag 0AG7, lemma-recover-tail-graded-module;
constructions.tex, Tag 01MT, lemma-apply-modules.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-finite-graded-module-section-tail).

The associated sheaf of each shift is specified by the chart interface of
`Proj.gradedModuleSheaf_exists`: injective chart maps with the prescribed fraction
ranges, scalar compatibility and canonical restriction formula. No new associated
sheaf construction is introduced. The maps to global sections are fixed by their
fraction formula, including their degree-zero scalar action.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u v

open CategoryTheory Opposite TopologicalSpace LocalizedModule HomogeneousLocalization

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Proj

/-- The canonical degree-n section map for a finite graded module is an isomorphism
in all sufficiently large degrees. The chart data specify the associated sheaf of
M(n), whose degree-d piece is M_(n+d); eta is the canonical scalar map, and gamma
is the canonical section map. Its scalar identity is expressed using ambient
representatives, so no auxiliary scalar instance or grading transport is chosen.

Source: Stacks Project, Tag 0AG7, lemma-recover-tail-graded-module, and Tag 01MT.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-finite-graded-module-section-tail)

Proof:
1. Choose the finite degree-one algebra generators f_i. Their standard opens cover
   Proj, and S is Noetherian by lem-weil-pbc-finite-type-algebra-noetherian.
   By lem-sfb-standard-proj-coherent-section-finiteness, Proj is Noetherian.
   Split finite module generators into homogeneous components, of degrees d_j.
2. The associated sheaf is quasi-coherent by
   lem-weil-pbc-proj-graded-module-sheaf-exists. On D_+(f_i) it is generated by
   x_j/f_i^d_j, also when d_j is negative. Apply
   lem-weil-pbc-quasi-coherent-finite-type-affine and pqf-lem-coherent-ft-locnoeth
   to obtain coherence.
3. Use lem-sfb-standard-proj-twist-tensor to identify its tensor twists with the
   sheaves of shifted modules. The canonical maps glue to a graded S-linear map
   M to N, the direct sum of all twisted global sections. Linearity holds on charts.
4. By lem-sfb-proj-section-module-reconstruction and
   lem-sc-p1-proj-tilde-functorial, the map M_(f_i) to N_(f_i) is inverse to the
   reconstruction map: the composite sends x/f_i^a to itself by the twist formula.
5. The nonnegative truncations M+ and N+ are finite: use
   lem-trf-noetherian-submodule-finitely-presented for M+ and
   lem-sfb-standard-proj-coherent-section-finiteness for N+. The kernel K and
   cokernel Q of the restricted map are finite graded modules, zero in negative
   degrees, whose degree-n pieces are its degreewise kernel and cokernel for n >= 0.
6. Nonnegative truncation does not change degree-zero localization at f_i: all
   fractions have numerators of nonnegative degree, and the fraction relation is
   unchanged. By lem-sc-graded-localization-exact, K_(f_i) and Q_(f_i) vanish.
7. For T = K or Q choose finite homogeneous generators t_j of degrees e_j >= 0.
   The zero fraction t_j/f_i^e_j gives f_i^b_ij t_j = 0 for some b_ij >= 1,
   by def-weil-pbc-module-localization-away. Nilpotent generators are allowed.
8. For n > max({0} union {e_j + sum_i b_ij}), expand each degree-n element in
   monomials in the f_i times t_j. One exponent is at least b_ij, so each term
   vanishes. With no algebra generators there are no positive-degree monomials;
   with T = 0 use the empty generating family and bound zero.
9. Choose n0 = 1 + max of the two bounds. The degree-n kernel and cokernel vanish
   for n >= n0. Thus the canonical map is bijective and S_0-linear. Composing
   with the shift/tensor comparison recovers exactly x maps to x/1 on every chart.
   This also treats empty Proj and modules with irrelevant-ideal torsion.
-/
theorem finite_graded_module_section_tail
    {S : Type u} [CommRing S] (𝒜 : ℕ → AddSubgroup S) [GradedRing 𝒜]
    [IsNoetherianRing (𝒜 0)]
    (hgen : ∃ (r : ℕ) (f : Fin r → S),
      (∀ i : Fin r, f i ∈ 𝒜 1) ∧ Algebra.adjoin (𝒜 0) (Set.range f) = ⊤)
    {M : Type v} [AddCommGroup M] [Module S M] [Module.Finite S M]
    (𝓜 : ℤ → AddSubgroup M) (h𝓜 : DirectSum.IsInternal 𝓜)
    (hsmul : ∀ (a : ℕ) (b : ℤ) (s : S) (x : M),
      s ∈ 𝒜 a → x ∈ 𝓜 b → s • x ∈ 𝓜 ((a : ℤ) + b)) :
    ∃ n0 : ℤ, 0 ≤ n0 ∧ ∀ n : ℤ, n0 ≤ n →
    ∃ (F : SheafOfModules.{max u v} (moduleRings (Proj 𝒜).toRingedSpace))
      (alpha : ∀ (f : S) (d : ℕ), 0 < d → f ∈ 𝒜 d →
        F.val.obj (op (basicOpen 𝒜 f)) →+ LocalizedModule.Away f M),
      (∀ (f : S) (d : ℕ) (hd : 0 < d) (hf : f ∈ 𝒜 d),
        Function.Injective (alpha f d hd hf) ∧
        Set.range (alpha f d hd hf) = degreeZeroFractions
          (fun k : ℕ ↦ (𝒜 k : Set S)) (fun k : ℕ ↦ (𝓜 (n + k) : Set M))
          (Submonoid.powers f)) ∧
      (∀ (f : S) (d : ℕ) (hd : 0 < d) (hf : f ∈ 𝒜 d)
        (r : HomogeneousLocalization.Away 𝒜 f)
        (s : F.val.obj (op (basicOpen 𝒜 f))),
        alpha f d hd hf (awayToSection 𝒜 f r • s) =
          algebraMap (HomogeneousLocalization.Away 𝒜 f) (Localization.Away f) r •
            alpha f d hd hf s) ∧
      (∀ (f g : S) (d b : ℕ) (hd : 0 < d) (hb : 0 < b)
        (hf : f ∈ 𝒜 d) (hg : g ∈ 𝒜 b) (inc : basicOpen 𝒜 g ≤ basicOpen 𝒜 f)
        (e k : ℕ) (a : S), 0 < e → a ∈ 𝒜 k → g ^ e = a * f →
        ∀ (m : ℕ) (y : M) (s : F.val.obj (op (basicOpen 𝒜 f))),
        alpha f d hd hf s = mk y (⟨f ^ m, ⟨m, rfl⟩⟩ : Submonoid.powers f) →
        alpha g b hb hg (F.val.map (homOfLE inc).op s) =
          mk (a ^ m • y) (⟨g ^ (e * m), ⟨e * m, rfl⟩⟩ : Submonoid.powers g)) ∧
    ∃ (eta : 𝒜 0 →+* (Proj 𝒜).presheaf.obj (op ⊤))
      (gamma : 𝓜 n →+ F.val.obj (op ⊤)),
      (∀ (r : 𝒜 0) (f : S) (d : ℕ) (hd : 0 < d) (hf : f ∈ 𝒜 d),
        (Proj 𝒜).presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : basicOpen 𝒜 f ≤ ⊤)).op (eta r) =
          awayToSection 𝒜 f (fromZeroRingHom 𝒜 _ r)) ∧
      (∀ (r : 𝒜 0) (x y : 𝓜 n), (y : M) = (r : S) • (x : M) →
        gamma y = eta r • gamma x) ∧
      (∀ (x : 𝓜 n) (f : S) (d : ℕ) (hd : 0 < d) (hf : f ∈ 𝒜 d),
        alpha f d hd hf
          (F.val.map (homOfLE (le_top : basicOpen 𝒜 f ≤ ⊤)).op (gamma x)) =
            mk (x : M) 1) ∧
      Function.Bijective gamma := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.Proj
